WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:08.629
Ally froze with fear. She had two choices: she could pretend she didn't hear whoever was behind her and walk away.

2
00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:11.451
Or, choice two, she could run away!

3
00:00:11.452 --> 00:00:15.034
But before she could do anything at all, the person stepped in front of her.

4
00:00:15.035 --> 00:00:18.214
Mateo's eyes were wide, and his jaw hung open.

5
00:00:18.215 --> 00:00:24.877
"Did what I think just happened really just happen? That was . . . Are you a . . . ?"

6
00:00:24.878 --> 00:00:29.182
"Please, Mateo, don't tell anyone what you saw," Ally pleaded.

7
00:00:29.183 --> 00:00:36.880
"My ship broke down. I need parts and fuel, and once I get them, I'm going to leave. I came to Earth in peace!"

8
00:00:36.881 --> 00:00:41.908
"I knew it," he murmured. "When I saw you onstage before . . ."

9
00:00:41.909 --> 00:00:54.252
"Please don't tell anyone!" Ally repeated. "It could put me in danger!"

10
00:00:54.253 --> 00:00:59.436
"I won't," Mateo said. "But I do have to say one thing."

11
00:00:59.437 --> 00:01:03.099
Ally gulped.

12
00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:06.528
"You were robbed!" he said.

13
00:01:06.529 --> 00:01:09.603
"Someone stole my pod?"

14
00:01:09.604 --> 00:01:16.674
"No." Mateo smiled. "You totally should have won first prize in the contest!"

15
00:01:16.675 --> 00:01:23.189
Ally laughed with relief. "Oh! I agree.

16
00:01:23.190 --> 00:01:27.358
So you're not mad at me for lying to you?"

17
00:01:27.359 --> 00:01:34.278
"No way," Mateo said. "I mean, how many people can say their good friend is an alien?"

18
00:01:34.279 --> 00:01:40.590
Touched, Ally put a hand on her heart. "You think of me as your good friend?"

19
00:01:40.591 --> 00:01:45.345
"We haven't known each other long, but you've been really helpful to Papi and me."

20
00:01:45.346 --> 00:01:50.704
Ally's eyes filled with tears. An Earthling was calling her a good friend!

21
00:01:50.705 --> 00:02:06.468
Her parents would be thrilled at all the peaceful cooperation she'd achieved on this planet.

22
00:02:06.469 --> 00:02:13.624
"I'll make you a deal," Mateo said. "Since I know your big secret, I'll tell you mine."

23
00:02:13.625 --> 00:02:17.352
"You don't have to do that," Ally said.

24
00:02:17.353 --> 00:02:21.469
"I want to," Mateo replied.

25
00:02:21.470 --> 00:02:27.120
"I've never told this to anyone. I know where my mom is.

26
00:02:27.121 --> 00:02:32.694
She texts me. She's trying to pursue a new career and live on her own.

27
00:02:32.695 --> 00:02:37.882
But she's worried if my dad knows, he'll try to convince her to come back home."

28
00:02:37.883 --> 00:02:44.802
"Wow, that's a huge secret," Ally said. "Thank you for trusting me with it."

29
00:02:44.803 --> 00:02:51.534
"Well, it's not quite as big as being an alien," Mateo said.

30
00:02:51.535 --> 00:02:55.525
"So where are these parts you need?"

31
00:02:55.526 --> 00:02:58.237
Ally got teary-eyed again.

32
00:02:58.238 --> 00:03:05.912
"I thought they were here in Sandville, but it turns out Dr. Lloyd lured my ship here. So . . ." She

33
00:03:05.913 --> 00:03:11.614
swallowed hard. "I don't know if I'll ever get home." Mateo

34
00:03:11.615 --> 00:03:13.911
put an arm around her shoulder. "I'll

35
00:03:13.912 --> 00:03:22.779
help you figure it out. For now, why don't we find the others and head back to the diner." As

36
00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:28.610
Ally and Mateo headed to the main hall, she told him all about Dr. Lloyd's discoveries. "His

37
00:03:28.611 --> 00:03:32.612
research has lots of inaccuracies," she said. "But

38
00:03:32.613 --> 00:03:38.980
he's not totally misinformed. And if he finds out about me, I bet he'll . . ." She

39
00:03:38.981 --> 00:03:49.199
swallowed hard again. "Try to use me for more research!" ***

40
00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:57.455
At the diner Barry was wiping down tables, and Flo and Ray were chatting behind the counter.

41
00:03:57.456 --> 00:04:03.184
"Hey, kids!" Ray greeted them with a big smile. "How was the convention?"

42
00:04:03.185 --> 00:04:08.103
"Interesting." Mateo traded glances with Ally.

43
00:04:08.104 --> 00:04:11.264
"How about some ice cream on the house?" Ray said.

44
00:04:11.265 --> 00:04:14.335
"Yes!" everyone said.

45
00:04:14.336 --> 00:04:17.383
"He's in a good mood," Mateo whispered to Ally.

46
00:04:17.384 --> 00:04:21.716
Ally nodded. Ray did seem happy, and she knew why:

47
00:04:21.717 --> 00:04:25.517
Ray's and Flo's thoughts were suddenly coming to her loud and clear.

48
00:04:25.518 --> 00:04:29.805
They were both thinking about how much they enjoyed each other's company.

49
00:04:29.806 --> 00:04:33.029
"I did make Ray happy," Ally thought.

50
00:04:33.030 --> 00:04:41.176
"I did it by hiring Flo!" It was another good deed that would impress her parents.

51
00:04:41.177 --> 00:04:45.674
Ally was about to dig into her bowl of ice cream when Barry came over.

52
00:04:45.675 --> 00:04:49.002
"When are you going to teach me that levitating trick?"

53
00:04:49.003 --> 00:04:53.966
"Why is he so desperate to learn that?" Ally thought, annoyed.

54
00:04:53.967 --> 00:05:01.197
She did a quick scan of his thoughts, but all she could see was an image of a man, likely his father, looking proud.

55
00:05:01.198 --> 00:05:06.069
She felt her heart soften. "I understand that feeling," she thought.

56
00:05:06.070 --> 00:05:09.227
"I want my parents to be proud of me too."

57
00:05:09.228 --> 00:05:15.714
"Soon, Barry." Ally held crossed fingers behind her back, the way humans did when telling white lies.

58
00:05:15.715 --> 00:05:19.085
For once Barry took that for an answer and walked away.

59
00:05:19.086 --> 00:05:21.886
Ally kept her fingers crossed for another minute.

60
00:05:21.887 --> 00:05:24.713
But it wasn't because she was about to tell another lie.

61
00:05:24.714 --> 00:05:30.418
It was because humans often crossed their fingers for another reason—luck.

62
00:05:30.419 --> 00:05:41.873
With Mateo's help, maybe she could figure out a way to get home soon.

